    {
      "id": 240982,
      "name": "doppelgangerung",
      "username": "doppelgangerung",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/doppelgangerung/{size}/1876_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-10-21T06:01:47.963Z",
      "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/5/590cf9c1ba27018b7c4af2cfbf874507faab9fbc.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/590cf9c1ba27018b7c4af2cfbf874507faab9fbc\" title=\"Screenshot_20211018-223450\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/590cf9c1ba27018b7c4af2cfbf874507faab9fbc_2_219x500.jpeg\" alt=\"Screenshot_20211018-223450\" data-base62-sha1=\"cHMihWDr1Gyl2RLJtQAFbx9ZzXu\" width=\"219\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/590cf9c1ba27018b7c4af2cfbf874507faab9fbc_2_219x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/590cf9c1ba27018b7c4af2cfbf874507faab9fbc_2_328x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/590cf9c1ba27018b7c4af2cfbf874507faab9fbc_2_438x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/5/590cf9c1ba27018b7c4af2cfbf874507faab9fbc_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot_20211018-223450</span><span class=\"informations\">1080×2460 186 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Damage prevention and mitigation was key in keeping the heroes alive long enough to defeat Dawn; a first round Elemental Exochassis and second round Flock’s Care helped blunt damage from Citizens Hammer, Assault, and of course, Dawn herself, allowing the team to concentrate their efforts on bringing her down before dropping enough lesser Citizens to make her flip. Omnitron-X tanked a lot of Elemental damage, eliminated Citizen Truth with a Defensive Blast, and helped get everyone else’s cards into play, Harpy got Harpy Hex and Applied Numerology into play, and plinked away at her targets of choice, Tachyon Experimented on herself and got off a timely Hypersonic Assault to shut down the villains’ damage for another round, and got off a 10-point Lightspeed Barrage, and Mr. Fixer’s Dual Crowbars allowed him to whack a secondary target first, then double dip on its damage bonus, along with the bonuses for Grease Monkey Fist and the more-helpful-than-annoying-for-a-change Taiga, to pummel Dawn until finishing her off with an Overdrive.</p>",
